  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194737/assets/70d961102240b0c48132baca8db0b77ed80ff8e0d3b7296bd5c727ab2f97dfd3.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $10+5\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg.",
  "worked_solution": "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=10+5\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 10+5\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 5\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 5 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $5.$",
